    "directions": [
      "Slather two rye bread with half the butter and place buttered side down on a plate. Spread the tops of these slices with half the Reuben Sauce. Lay the corned beef and pastrami on top of the dressing, followed by the sauerkraut and Gruyère.",
      "Spread the remaining two bread slices with the remaining Reuben Sauce. Place them dressing side down on the sandwiches and spread the tops with the remaining butter.",
      "If using a contact grill, preheat it. Grill the sandwiches until the bread crisps and melts, and the meats are hot, 3 to 5 minutes. Alternatively, if using a skillet, griddle, or plancha, heat it over medium-high heat. Add the sandwiches and place a grill press on top. Cook until the bread crisps and browns, the cheese melts, and the meats are hot, 3 to 5 minutes per side, carefully turning with a spatula.",
      "Cut each sandwich in half on the diagonal and serve at once."
    ],
